1
00:00:13,540 --> 00:01:27,260
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,486 --> 00:02:08,486
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:02:12,075 --> 00:02:14,595
Let go of me, let go!

4
00:02:28,289 --> 00:02:32,289
Are you out of your breath...

5
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,750
... because you are fighting
for freedom, Osman?

6
00:02:36,098 --> 00:02:42,978
I will kill you with my
own hands, Dündar Bey!

7
00:03:15,369 --> 00:03:20,819
What is it, are you going after
what is mine, Osman Bey?

8
00:03:38,839 --> 00:03:39,969
No.

9
00:03:45,370 --> 00:03:50,790
Did you really think you could
take Genghis Khan's legacy from me?

10
00:04:28,369 --> 00:04:31,759
Come on, you idiots, come on, hurry!

11
00:04:32,337 --> 00:04:36,337
If something happens to this woman,
even I can't save you from Balgay's wrath.

12
00:04:37,816 --> 00:04:39,096
As you say, Cerkutay.

13
00:04:39,182 --> 00:04:41,522
Take the woman to
Balgay without hurting her.

14
00:05:06,649 --> 00:05:10,649
You follow me, we have some
unfinished business.

15
00:05:13,686 --> 00:05:15,516
Osman Bey.

16
00:05:27,232 --> 00:05:28,722
Dündar Bey!

17
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:34,480
You became allies with the
Mongols for my father's place!

18
00:05:35,659 --> 00:05:39,379
You made your son, Batur
partner for your treason!

19
00:05:40,852 --> 00:05:42,152
Enough, Osman.

20
00:05:43,149 --> 00:05:44,329
Enough.

21
00:05:49,101 --> 00:05:55,471
You did all this because of your
irresponsible, reckless, childish acts.

22
00:05:56,484 --> 00:06:00,484
You will pay for your doings, not Kayıs!

23
00:06:04,664 --> 00:06:08,954
You will burn in the fire of
rebellion that you started.

24
00:06:15,604 --> 00:06:20,644
I will make my father's tent your grave!

25
00:06:25,568 --> 00:06:30,878
Wolves are with the wolves.
Jackals are with the jackals.

26
00:06:39,498 --> 00:06:41,428
Jackals' reign ends...

27
00:06:49,118 --> 00:06:51,898
... when wolves stand up!

28
00:07:05,313 --> 00:07:09,313
I will kill you with my
own hands, Dündar Bey!

29
00:07:16,128 --> 00:07:20,128
This Tent is ruled
with Genghis Khan's laws...

30
00:07:20,845 --> 00:07:23,895
... not with Oguz's traditions.

31
00:07:25,290 --> 00:07:29,750
You will not live until you see the
consequences of your treason, Osman Bey.

32
00:07:44,977 --> 00:07:47,227
- Balgay-
- Later, Kongar.

33
00:07:48,546 --> 00:07:50,306
Die, Osman!

34
00:07:50,934 --> 00:07:54,934
Freedom or death!

35
00:08:05,832 --> 00:08:07,272
Die!

36
00:08:17,916 --> 00:08:19,346
Die, Osman!

37
00:08:29,414 --> 00:08:31,964
I came here to take what is Geyhatu's.

38
00:08:56,080 --> 00:09:00,080
I was able to take Genghis
Khan's laws from Osman's hands.

39
00:09:03,764 --> 00:09:06,664
The laws are my gift to Geyhatu.

40
00:09:33,375 --> 00:09:35,145
And the blessed dagger.

41
00:10:08,001 --> 00:10:09,181
Geyhatu...

42
00:10:10,785 --> 00:10:15,505
... won't leave this victory
of yours without a prize.

43
00:10:16,354 --> 00:10:18,304
Don't you worry, Balgay.

44
00:10:26,238 --> 00:10:27,648
Is this Osman?

45
00:10:28,103 --> 00:10:28,863
Yes.

46
00:11:12,395 --> 00:11:15,795
My Allah, don't let me perish
in the hands of the enemy.

47
00:11:15,909 --> 00:11:18,229
Let me die while fighting.

48
00:11:22,819 --> 00:11:26,819
Osman Bey is a prisoner of Geyhatu.

49
00:11:31,068 --> 00:11:35,068
We will take him to Konya.

50
00:11:36,739 --> 00:11:37,549
Soldiers.

51
00:11:39,576 --> 00:11:41,376
Take Osman Bey to the cart.

52
00:11:43,473 --> 00:11:44,883
Cauterize his wounds.

53
00:11:46,882 --> 00:11:49,052
No one will get near him.

54
00:12:15,427 --> 00:12:16,417
Balgay.

55
00:12:18,208 --> 00:12:19,428
Come with me to the tent.

56
00:12:20,306 --> 00:12:22,056
I have news from Geyhatu.

57
00:12:27,943 --> 00:12:29,203
You should come too.

58
00:12:36,387 --> 00:12:37,437
My Osman!

59
00:13:31,088 --> 00:13:31,898
Stop!

60
00:13:35,087 --> 00:13:35,927
Stop!

61
00:13:41,930 --> 00:13:43,750
You are the banner lord now.

62
00:13:44,889 --> 00:13:48,169
Commander Balgay decided it was suitable.

63
00:13:50,556 --> 00:13:54,776
Nothing is suitable if
Geyhatu is not informed.

64
00:13:59,056 --> 00:14:02,336
But, if Balgay decided it...

65
00:14:03,670 --> 00:14:05,290
... he must know something.

66
00:14:12,010 --> 00:14:13,830
I will have my eyes on you...

67
00:14:16,102 --> 00:14:18,922
... and my ears in your Tent...

68
00:14:19,463 --> 00:14:20,533
Dündar.

69
00:14:22,982 --> 00:14:24,232
Now go.

70
00:14:42,223 --> 00:14:47,333
I want to take Genghis
Khan's laws to Konya personally.

71
00:14:47,991 --> 00:14:53,951
Don't worry, Geyhatu will know you are the
one who found and give the laws to him.

72
00:14:54,182 --> 00:14:56,782
What is it with taking Osman to Konya?

73
00:14:57,146 --> 00:15:02,186
Geyhatu wants to interrogate
Osman to find out how he got the laws.

74
00:15:02,872 --> 00:15:04,882
He is not your prisoner anymore.

75
00:15:08,958 --> 00:15:11,988
Are you afraid of something, Balgay?

76
00:15:55,326 --> 00:15:59,326
Osman, my Osman, Osman!

77
00:16:12,842 --> 00:16:14,042
Ya Allah!

78
00:16:39,921 --> 00:16:42,301
Stay away! We don't want trouble!

79
00:16:42,398 --> 00:16:44,908
Osman will be taken away!

80
00:17:08,590 --> 00:17:10,830
I am talking to you, Balgay.

81
00:17:17,329 --> 00:17:19,669
Is there something that concerns you?

82
00:17:23,607 --> 00:17:26,957
I don't have any
concerns, Commander Köni.

83
00:17:28,492 --> 00:17:34,562
Geyhatu should know that I am
ready to die for him, that's enough.

84
00:18:01,757 --> 00:18:03,767
What if Osman tell Geyhatu everything?

85
00:18:06,273 --> 00:18:10,273
Kill Köni and his soldiers.

86
00:18:11,492 --> 00:18:15,152
Take Osman and the laws to me.

87
00:18:15,981 --> 00:18:17,861
As you command, Commander Balgay.

88
00:18:44,054 --> 00:18:45,314
Show yourself!

89
00:19:12,478 --> 00:19:13,798
My Allah...

90
00:19:15,391 --> 00:19:16,931
... give me strength.

91
00:19:56,218 --> 00:20:00,648
Brothers, don't you despair
brothers and sisters!

92
00:20:03,859 --> 00:20:06,449
Stand strong, Kayı Tent!

93
00:20:06,493 --> 00:20:08,203
We will stand strong!

94
00:20:09,141 --> 00:20:11,681
We will stand strong, Kayı Tent!

95
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:15,730
No one can bend our knees!

96
00:20:17,853 --> 00:20:21,853
Even if they make all
the world a prison...

97
00:20:22,442 --> 00:20:25,492
... we will never give up our cause!

98
00:20:27,823 --> 00:20:31,823
Freedom or death!

99
00:20:33,016 --> 00:20:40,186
Allahu Akbar!
[Allah is the greatest!]

100
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:55,180
Dündar Bey.

101
00:20:57,746 --> 00:20:59,356
Wait for my word.

102
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:05,020
Because our enemies grow in number.

103
00:21:06,652 --> 00:21:11,142
Don't you ever forget that I am the one
who gave you the rank of banner lord.

104
00:21:12,172 --> 00:21:15,742
My loyalty to you knows no limits, Balgay.

105
00:21:24,202 --> 00:21:25,482
Show yourself!

106
00:21:27,876 --> 00:21:28,916
Where are you?

107
00:21:34,294 --> 00:21:36,044
Show yourself, where are you?

108
00:22:04,911 --> 00:22:06,341
Batur.

109
00:22:07,641 --> 00:22:09,101
Batur!

110
00:22:09,365 --> 00:22:11,145
I thought you were a man!

111
00:22:11,585 --> 00:22:13,565
But there is a snake in your heart!

112
00:22:15,925 --> 00:22:17,635
Shame on you, Batur.

113
00:22:18,062 --> 00:22:20,172
You make Kayı Tent
bleed with your treason!

114
00:22:20,766 --> 00:22:24,406
Bamsı Bey, Abdurrahman Gazi...

115
00:22:25,140 --> 00:22:32,170
Osman saw you as a brother, he risked
his life for you, all my efforts for you-

116
00:22:32,651 --> 00:22:39,171
Stop, woman, do you think my son is alone,
that you judge without listening?

117
00:22:39,285 --> 00:22:40,895
I did all this.

118
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:42,210
Me.

119
00:22:44,958 --> 00:22:46,428
Your Bey did it.

120
00:22:49,199 --> 00:22:54,569
Your banner lord, that
you dislike, disobey!

121
00:22:55,223 --> 00:22:58,593
Are you hearing your
own words, Dündar Bey?

122
00:22:58,683 --> 00:23:01,033
I am, I am.

123
00:23:01,683 --> 00:23:06,673
How do you think Köni
came here, Bamsı Bey?

124
00:23:08,421 --> 00:23:14,341
Who planned this game, who do you
think repelled all those jackals around?

125
00:23:19,173 --> 00:23:20,103
I did it.

126
00:23:24,817 --> 00:23:33,347
I personally sent word to the Mongolian
governor in Konya, made the two dogs fight!

127
00:23:34,439 --> 00:23:35,779
Now...

128
00:23:37,155 --> 00:23:44,765
... that dog, Balgay will get angry,
and they will enter a battle.

129
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:51,750
I got nothing else to do
to keep my Tent safe.

130
00:23:54,302 --> 00:23:59,787
If something happens to Osman, if they kill
him in Konya, what will you do, Dündar Bey?

131
00:23:59,787 --> 00:24:02,362
Then what will you do, Dündar Bey?
If something happens to Osman, if they kill
him in Konya, what will you do, Dündar Bey?

132
00:24:02,362 --> 00:24:02,607
Then what will you do, Dündar Bey?

133
00:24:02,607 --> 00:24:04,297
They promised.

134
00:24:04,944 --> 00:24:06,724
They swore!

135
00:24:07,559 --> 00:24:11,559
They won't hurt Osman.
They'll just interrogate him.

136
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:14,617
They'll just interrogate him.

137
00:24:16,584 --> 00:24:21,904
We got it. You're not a traitor.

138
00:24:24,983 --> 00:24:30,173
But you're naive, Dündar. Naive!

139
00:24:32,879 --> 00:24:35,059
How can you trust the Mongols?

140
00:24:36,932 --> 00:24:39,402
How can you trust the Mongols?

141
00:24:40,831 --> 00:24:46,531
Not just Batur. Shame on both of you!

142
00:24:48,860 --> 00:24:50,750
Shame on you too!

143
00:25:01,107 --> 00:25:07,107
If something happens to Osman,
then I'll become an eagle and...

144
00:25:07,107 --> 00:25:12,647
... dismember you with my own claws.
Know that, Dündar Bey!

145
00:25:12,647 --> 00:25:15,337
Listen to me carefully, Selcan Hatun.

146
00:25:15,952 --> 00:25:19,032
You're not looking at the old Dündar.

147
00:25:19,686 --> 00:25:24,086
After your smallest mistake,
I'll rip your claws off and...

148
00:25:24,086 --> 00:25:27,686
... break your wings. Know that.

149
00:25:54,497 --> 00:25:55,697
Giddy up!

150
00:26:34,369 --> 00:26:36,829
Kayı Tent loves you very much.

151
00:26:37,078 --> 00:26:39,468
They love fighting the cruel more.

152
00:26:41,243 --> 00:26:43,793
You look like you're sure
that you'll return.

153
00:26:45,534 --> 00:26:48,334
Who said Geyhatu will release you?

154
00:26:48,334 --> 00:26:53,234
You came here without knowing
who we are, Köni.

155
00:26:54,984 --> 00:26:59,714
We have hejira within our migration,
reclusion within our sorrow...

156
00:27:00,373 --> 00:27:03,923
... testimony within our revenge.

157
00:27:52,219 --> 00:27:53,959
- Bamsı Bey!
- Sons!

158
00:27:53,959 --> 00:27:55,309
Where is that dog Balgay?

159
00:27:55,309 --> 00:28:00,009
Balgay didn't take Osman.
It's Geyhatu's helper Köni.

160
00:28:00,273 --> 00:28:03,623
So Geyhatu is aware of Genghis' Laws.

161
00:28:04,564 --> 00:28:06,924
So we've found a new enemy.

162
00:28:06,924 --> 00:28:09,704
It doesn't matter if Genghis
comes out of his grave.

163
00:28:09,704 --> 00:28:14,124
We'll not let those infidels decide
Osman's fate! Come on valiants!

164
00:28:45,243 --> 00:28:46,803
My Osman!

165
00:29:31,816 --> 00:29:33,796
The prisoner is running away!

166
00:29:36,613 --> 00:29:38,043
Get him!

167
00:29:42,898 --> 00:29:44,458
Köni!

168
00:29:49,948 --> 00:29:51,468
Kongar!

169
00:29:53,629 --> 00:29:55,239
Kill them all!

170
00:30:29,931 --> 00:30:31,661
Where is Osman?

171
00:30:34,601 --> 00:30:40,241
- Where is the Genghis Khans' law?
- Geyhatu will make you pay for this!

172
00:30:40,241 --> 00:30:44,121
There is no one left to inform
Geyhatu, Köni.

173
00:30:44,121 --> 00:30:46,441
You'll die too!

174
00:30:48,309 --> 00:30:54,229
You're wrong! Osman will be your end!

175
00:30:54,229 --> 00:30:57,269
So you let Osman take the laws too, fool!

176
00:31:02,149 --> 00:31:05,729
Find Osman! If you can't,
I'll rip your hearts out!

177
00:33:35,455 --> 00:33:39,455
These are Balgay's men. They killed
Köni too.

178
00:33:40,523 --> 00:33:42,623
Osman Bey is nowhere to be seen either.

179
00:33:51,928 --> 00:33:55,028
Bamsı Bey. Isn't this dagger yours?

180
00:33:57,792 --> 00:34:00,342
It's mine. Where did you find this?

181
00:34:00,342 --> 00:34:03,282
There's a dead body by the cart. I took
it from his neck.

182
00:34:04,422 --> 00:34:10,362
Good. So Osman managed to run away before
Balgay's dogs arrived.

183
00:34:14,484 --> 00:34:18,975
Good. Good. Come on, lions. We need to
find Osman before those infidels!

184
00:34:18,975 --> 00:34:21,475
We won't let dogs get our lion, my Bey.

185
00:34:21,475 --> 00:34:24,885
- We won't. Come on, valiants.
- Let's go.

186
00:36:51,525 --> 00:36:56,695
Until I get to smell your silky hair,
wrap this scarf on your head.

187
00:36:58,591 --> 00:37:02,591
Every time I pray to Allah almighty,
your name is in my prayers.

188
00:37:03,699 --> 00:37:08,849
I pray that Allah resigns us to
each other for eternity.

189
00:37:09,831 --> 00:37:11,181
Osman!

190
00:37:12,908 --> 00:37:15,588
Forgive me.

191
00:37:19,228 --> 00:37:23,068
I left you alone in your hard days.

192
00:37:24,729 --> 00:37:26,109
Forgive me.

193
00:40:05,749 --> 00:40:07,399
Alaca!

194
00:40:18,224 --> 00:40:19,804
Alaca!

195
00:41:38,686 --> 00:41:41,376
Don't be scared. You're safe.

196
00:41:48,994 --> 00:41:52,294
- Who are you?
- Don't worry about who I am.

197
00:41:53,852 --> 00:41:56,702
Your wound needs to be cleaned and seared.

198
00:41:56,936 --> 00:41:58,916
You need to hold on.

199
00:42:44,500 --> 00:42:45,840
Bala!

200
00:42:48,193 --> 00:42:51,863
Bala, where are you?
Where are you, Bala?

201
00:43:05,542 --> 00:43:08,542
Where are you?
Where are you?

202
00:43:58,922 --> 00:44:02,672
Alaca! Where is my Bala?

203
00:44:03,680 --> 00:44:05,630
Where is my Bala?

204
00:44:07,507 --> 00:44:09,197
Where is she?

205
00:44:56,490 --> 00:45:00,050
There are two guests at
my traceless house today.

206
00:45:01,040 --> 00:45:02,620
Who are you?

207
00:45:03,403 --> 00:45:04,913
I'm l--

208
00:45:06,973 --> 00:45:09,153
I'm looking for someone.

209
00:45:09,514 --> 00:45:11,034
My horse is by the stable.

210
00:45:11,034 --> 00:45:12,254
Osman!

211
00:45:24,799 --> 00:45:26,289
Osman!

212
00:45:28,281 --> 00:45:31,381
- Bala!
- Osman!

213
00:45:36,824 --> 00:45:41,674
What did they do to you? Tell me, my dear.
What did they do to you?

214
00:45:42,249 --> 00:45:45,389
Bala! Tell me! Who did this to you?

215
00:45:46,314 --> 00:45:48,964
Who did this to you?

216
00:45:50,812 --> 00:45:54,812
I'm okay. Who did this?

217
00:45:55,556 --> 00:45:59,066
Tell me! Tell me and
I'll go rip his heart out!

218
00:46:00,170 --> 00:46:01,960
Cerkutay!

219
00:46:03,261 --> 00:46:05,531
They crossed my path.

220
00:46:10,663 --> 00:46:14,663
Son! Allow me for a second.

221
00:46:16,834 --> 00:46:19,814
Son! It should not cool down.

222
00:46:52,854 --> 00:46:56,304
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

223
00:47:03,952 --> 00:47:07,022
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

224
00:47:11,633 --> 00:47:14,693
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

225
00:48:02,846 --> 00:48:04,876
Will she live?

226
00:48:07,434 --> 00:48:09,424
Tell me. Will she live?

227
00:48:09,940 --> 00:48:12,990
I don't know. I did my best.

228
00:48:17,089 --> 00:48:19,289
The rest is for Allah to decide.

229
00:48:23,448 --> 00:48:25,258
You're not okay.

230
00:48:26,771 --> 00:48:28,411
Go lay there.

231
00:48:34,544 --> 00:48:36,444
Those cruel dogs!

232
00:48:39,463 --> 00:48:42,613
I'll give you the worst of deaths!

233
00:48:53,108 --> 00:48:54,608
Mother!

234
00:48:55,747 --> 00:48:57,827
She is my dearest.

235
00:48:59,098 --> 00:49:01,678
Don't let her fade away.

236
00:49:03,921 --> 00:49:06,811
Save her. Save her.

237
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:11,150
My Allah, help this poor servant of yours.

238
00:49:11,917 --> 00:49:15,007
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

239
00:49:36,829 --> 00:49:39,999
"May the peace and mercy of
Allah be with you."

240
00:49:40,775 --> 00:49:44,005
"May the peace and mercy of
Allah be with you."

241
00:49:49,669 --> 00:49:52,999
My Allah, keeper of everything...

242
00:49:53,979 --> 00:49:57,269
You command everything.

243
00:49:57,944 --> 00:50:04,424
You're capable. You possess real
power and potency.

244
00:50:06,089 --> 00:50:12,889
Ya Rab! Your people are in misery!

245
00:50:13,734 --> 00:50:17,324
Not only the cruel and intruders...

246
00:50:18,084 --> 00:50:21,824
... unrest and disunion also
captured them.

247
00:50:23,017 --> 00:50:27,517
We forgot about the greatest thing
that held us together.

248
00:50:28,320 --> 00:50:31,080
Muslim Brotherhood.

249
00:50:32,317 --> 00:50:35,397
We lost trust for each other.

250
00:50:36,471 --> 00:50:41,431
We gave in to our desires.

251
00:50:43,848 --> 00:50:47,048
My Rab, who knows everything!

252
00:50:48,307 --> 00:50:53,267
Clean our hearts' dirt with
the light of Islam.

253
00:50:54,105 --> 00:50:58,105
Enlighten us. Forgive us.

254
00:51:00,204 --> 00:51:05,274
Allow us to be strong
against infidelity...

255
00:51:06,269 --> 00:51:08,989
... the cruel and the devil's tricks.

256
00:51:10,438 --> 00:51:16,918
My Allah! Make us go through
Sirat al-Mustaqim.

257
00:51:18,212 --> 00:51:21,382
Allow us to be like those who always
follow the right path...

258
00:51:21,382 --> 00:51:25,272
... and die for this cause.

259
00:51:27,365 --> 00:51:29,445
Ya Rab!

260
00:51:30,466 --> 00:51:36,286
Scatter our darkness into the courtesy of
the name El Fettah...

261
00:51:37,598 --> 00:51:41,778
... allow us to destroy infidelity.

262
00:51:42,841 --> 00:51:47,151
To us, to those Muslims
waiting for hope...

263
00:51:48,316 --> 00:51:51,236
... to the poor waiting for
the good news...

264
00:51:51,818 --> 00:51:54,788
... allow us to rise anew.

265
00:52:05,376 --> 00:52:07,176
Greetings, friend.

266
00:52:07,934 --> 00:52:11,434
Aleyküm Selam. What is it, Bamsı Bey?

267
00:52:12,106 --> 00:52:17,246
Friend, Geyhatu's men came from Konya
to take Osman.

268
00:52:17,437 --> 00:52:21,437
Osman ran away from them,
but now we can't find him.

269
00:52:21,539 --> 00:52:24,909
As if the ground swallowed him.

270
00:52:28,028 --> 00:52:31,408
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

271
00:52:37,012 --> 00:52:41,592
Bala Hatun is also lost.
We're looking for her everywhere.

272
00:52:41,592 --> 00:52:45,932
Do you think something happened to them?
What if the Mongols got them again?

273
00:52:53,081 --> 00:52:55,591
The things which saved Yusuf
from the well...

274
00:52:56,244 --> 00:52:58,364
... Ibrahim from fire...

275
00:52:59,692 --> 00:53:02,732
... İsmail from knives...

276
00:53:04,272 --> 00:53:08,272
... is both faith and effort, Bamsı Bey.

277
00:53:10,357 --> 00:53:14,357
There's no time to stop.
We shall go look for them.

278
00:53:15,669 --> 00:53:18,919
We take the measures
and let Allah decide it's fate.

279
00:53:19,197 --> 00:53:22,077
- Thank you.
- Thank you, friend. Here.

280
00:53:22,281 --> 00:53:26,281
Come on, lions! Let's go!

281
00:53:28,681 --> 00:53:31,471
Where are you, Bala? Where are you?

282
00:53:42,957 --> 00:53:46,957
- What happened here, Gonca Hatun?
- They had a battle, Pehlivan Dervish!

283
00:53:49,974 --> 00:53:52,224
Blood everywhere!

284
00:54:02,068 --> 00:54:05,518
I found the fardel over there!
There is someone's things inside.

285
00:54:05,518 --> 00:54:07,708
But nothing from Bala Hatun.

286
00:54:07,708 --> 00:54:10,198
Bala! Bala!

287
00:54:17,633 --> 00:54:20,703
These ornaments! They are Bala's.

288
00:54:21,090 --> 00:54:26,260
Friends! Keep looking. I'll go to the
Kayı Tent. I need to find Selcan Hatun.

289
00:54:26,260 --> 00:54:27,990
- Okay.
- Good bye.

290
00:54:27,990 --> 00:54:29,590
You too.

291
00:54:47,642 --> 00:54:51,862
Men of my Tent!
Çetin Alp will take you somewhere safe.

292
00:54:52,757 --> 00:54:56,177
And we'll go up to the mountains and
light the fire of rebellion.

293
00:54:56,683 --> 00:55:02,023
We won't rest until we kick those
Mongols who invade our lands!

294
00:55:02,023 --> 00:55:05,953
We're not looking for rest, Samsa Bey!
Don't look at our ages.

295
00:55:06,408 --> 00:55:10,268
We have breaths powerful enough
to disperse nine armies in one shout.

296
00:55:17,036 --> 00:55:19,926
You gave up on your chance
of testimony, Sazak Bey.

297
00:55:20,816 --> 00:55:22,666
Now it's time for us to fight.

298
00:55:22,666 --> 00:55:25,616
May Allah not let you die in your sleep.

299
00:55:25,776 --> 00:55:27,086
Amin.

300
00:55:29,456 --> 00:55:33,456
First Allah, then you will take care of
the men, women and children, Çetin Alp.

301
00:55:34,538 --> 00:55:36,848
- Thank you, my Bey!
- Thank you.

302
00:55:43,846 --> 00:55:46,626
My men, standing still like mountains!

303
00:55:47,503 --> 00:55:50,413
You have my blessings. I expect the same.

304
00:55:50,413 --> 00:55:52,843
You have our blessings, my Bey!

305
00:55:53,984 --> 00:56:02,684
- Long live Samsa Bey!
- Long live Samsa Bey!

306
00:56:19,105 --> 00:56:25,075
You shall fall victim to
the dark spirits' wrath, Cergutay!

307
00:56:30,046 --> 00:56:33,576
How can you let a wounded
Hatun run away from you?

308
00:56:33,576 --> 00:56:36,246
How can you be such a fool?

309
00:56:37,601 --> 00:56:39,831
You'll pay for this!

310
00:56:47,883 --> 00:56:50,703
- Did you take care of it?
- Commander Balgay...

311
00:56:51,345 --> 00:56:55,345
I killed Köni and his soldiers. They are
no longer a threat for us.

312
00:56:55,345 --> 00:56:59,915
Good. What about Osman?
Genghis Khan's laws?

313
00:57:00,385 --> 00:57:03,765
When I arrived, Osman had already left.

314
00:57:05,404 --> 00:57:09,944
Commander Balgay. Osman ran away
with Genghis Khans' laws.

315
00:57:09,944 --> 00:57:12,574
I sent my soldiers after him.

316
00:57:14,848 --> 00:57:19,268
Osman is wounded and alone. We'll
eventually find him, Commander Balgay.

317
00:57:20,210 --> 00:57:25,930
You'll tell Geyhatu that
his soldiers killed Osman.

318
00:57:26,744 --> 00:57:31,804
Send a messenger to Konya.
Tell what happened as I said.

319
00:57:31,804 --> 00:57:33,924
As you wish, Balgay.

320
00:57:39,179 --> 00:57:42,689
For the wrath of the spirits...

321
00:57:43,208 --> 00:57:48,938
Erlik Khan's curse to Osman...

322
00:58:05,509 --> 00:58:07,889
Call Zöhre here.

323
00:58:08,903 --> 00:58:11,533
I want her to come here tomorrow,
secretly.

324
00:58:11,929 --> 00:58:14,519
Dündar shouldn't know this.

325
00:58:15,209 --> 00:58:25,899
She'll tell me where Geyhatu heard that
I had Genghis Khans' laws.

326
00:58:27,283 --> 00:58:30,393
Come on! What are you waiting for?

327
00:58:45,702 --> 00:58:48,702
Osman!

328
00:58:57,021 --> 00:59:01,551
So Samsa climbed the mountains
and rebelled against Balgay?

329
00:59:02,648 --> 00:59:06,648
He took his Tent's men, women, and
children to somewhere safe.

330
00:59:07,969 --> 00:59:12,819
And tomorrow he will go to
Şahin Hill with his Alps.

331
00:59:13,428 --> 00:59:18,038
Brave enough to fight Balgay with
a handful of Alps...

332
00:59:18,416 --> 00:59:22,416
... dumb enough to think that he'll
win this battle.

333
00:59:23,997 --> 00:59:29,227
Miserable enough to deserve to die
with Balgay's grudge.

334
00:59:34,983 --> 00:59:40,123
How did Balgay know that Samsa will
go the Şahin Hill tomorrow?

335
00:59:43,358 --> 00:59:46,628
This has one answer, Master Yannis.

336
00:59:46,628 --> 00:59:51,978
Balgay must have bought one
of Samsa's Beys.

337
00:59:54,600 --> 01:00:02,750
We have to put a spy among
Balgay's commanders.

338
01:00:04,244 --> 01:00:07,234
I'll do what is necessary, Sofia.

339
01:00:09,506 --> 01:00:13,936
- Who do you have in mind?
- Everyone in this world has a price.

340
01:00:15,098 --> 01:00:16,978
Or a weakness.

341
01:00:22,723 --> 01:00:24,433
Master Yannis.

342
01:00:26,290 --> 01:00:30,750
Osman escaped from Geyhatu's
soldiers, Salvador.

343
01:00:32,474 --> 01:00:34,474
I'm not surprised.

344
01:00:35,106 --> 01:00:37,836
Osman is like oil.

345
01:00:38,549 --> 01:00:40,779
No one can hold him.

346
01:00:40,779 --> 01:00:47,359
To deal with Osman, one needs to separate
his head from his body.

347
01:00:48,548 --> 01:00:52,938
This is the right time for you to
take us where...

348
01:00:52,938 --> 01:00:55,118
... he and his Alps are hiding, Salvador.

349
01:00:55,118 --> 01:00:59,988
Make sure Osman is there when
we ambush them.

350
01:01:01,934 --> 01:01:04,494
I'll be commanding the soldiers.

351
01:01:08,037 --> 01:01:11,547
And I'll be with you, Princess Sofia.

352
01:01:12,383 --> 01:01:15,043
My valiant warrior Salvador.

353
01:01:15,434 --> 01:01:19,124
Now go, start preparing.

354
01:01:26,144 --> 01:01:33,304
You will capture Osman, Sofia. You will
take Genghis Khan's laws.

355
01:01:34,015 --> 01:01:38,005
Balgay shouldn't come to the ambush.
Do you understand?

356
01:01:38,005 --> 01:01:40,225
Don't worry, Master Yannis.

357
01:02:12,073 --> 01:02:14,503
- Selcan Hatun!
- I hope nothing's wrong!

358
01:02:14,503 --> 01:02:17,653
- Bala! She's lost.
- What do you mean she's lost.

359
01:02:17,653 --> 01:02:20,853
She said she'll be meeting with you.
I said I should come too.

360
01:02:20,853 --> 01:02:23,693
I don't want you to go alone, I said.

361
01:02:23,693 --> 01:02:26,963
She didn't listen. She went.
She didn't return.

362
01:02:26,963 --> 01:02:29,163
Dervishes are looking for here everwhere.

363
01:02:29,163 --> 01:02:31,343
No one saw or heard of her.

364
01:02:31,343 --> 01:02:34,443
Look what happened! Are there no traces?

365
01:02:35,057 --> 01:02:38,817
We found a fardel. But the things inside
are not Bala's.

366
01:02:39,245 --> 01:02:41,395
They are men's clothes.

367
01:02:44,160 --> 01:02:45,700
Zöhre!

368
01:02:45,700 --> 01:02:48,510
There were bloodstains where
we found the fardel.

369
01:02:48,510 --> 01:02:52,980
There was a fight for sure.
We found Bala's silver ornaments.

370
01:02:55,067 --> 01:02:59,157
Selcan Hatun! I'm begging you,
we should tell Osman Bey.

371
01:02:59,157 --> 01:03:01,277
No one else can find Bala.

372
01:03:01,572 --> 01:03:04,872
Osman! My Osman!

373
01:03:39,345 --> 01:03:41,105
Osman...

374
01:03:41,780 --> 01:03:43,290
Bala...

375
01:03:52,729 --> 01:03:54,329
Osman...

376
01:03:55,442 --> 01:03:56,852
Bala...

377
01:03:57,041 --> 01:03:59,071
She can't hear you.

378
01:04:00,511 --> 01:04:02,721
She's in another world right now.

379
01:04:21,487 --> 01:04:22,887
Drink.

380
01:04:24,240 --> 01:04:26,450
You need strength.

381
01:04:31,038 --> 01:04:37,488
It's not enough for you. Wait.
I had some jerky.

382
01:04:49,916 --> 01:04:52,366
She'll live, right, mother?

383
01:04:56,442 --> 01:04:57,732
She'll be okay, right?

384
01:04:57,732 --> 01:05:00,292
Blind love...

385
01:05:03,710 --> 01:05:07,070
You escaped death, and you're still
thinking about her.

386
01:05:10,417 --> 01:05:12,467
She'll live, hopefully.

387
01:05:15,418 --> 01:05:19,538
If she goes, half of my heart goes too.

388
01:05:21,421 --> 01:05:25,461
Then even if I set the whole world
on fire...

389
01:05:26,460 --> 01:05:29,290
... my anger for those who did this to her
will not go away.

390
01:05:29,290 --> 01:05:31,940
Your heart is strong like your arms.

391
01:05:33,647 --> 01:05:36,777
Such a heart is needed for such a love.

392
01:05:38,402 --> 01:05:41,592
Tell me. Where are you from, Osman Bey?

393
01:05:44,909 --> 01:05:49,959
From the Kayıs. How do you know my name?

394
01:05:50,309 --> 01:05:52,869
She kept saying Osman.

395
01:05:53,555 --> 01:05:55,555
It's obvious that it's you.

396
01:05:58,225 --> 01:06:01,475
Who are you? Where are you from?

397
01:06:01,475 --> 01:06:03,895
They call me Elif Hatun.

398
01:06:06,455 --> 01:06:10,065
If you have no friends or relatives,
no one calls your name.

399
01:06:15,023 --> 01:06:17,303
Why are you living in this cave?

400
01:06:17,996 --> 01:06:20,176
Isn't it hard being alone?

401
01:06:20,176 --> 01:06:26,316
I don't like people. I don't like to
expect things from servants of Allah.

402
01:06:27,066 --> 01:06:29,876
I ran away to here years ago.

403
01:06:29,876 --> 01:06:33,456
There is nothing but peace.

404
01:06:36,058 --> 01:06:38,538
Not just one, but two people.

405
01:06:38,538 --> 01:06:42,708
Wounded too. We broke your
peace, mother Elif.

406
01:06:45,876 --> 01:06:50,206
May Allah bless you. You healed us.

407
01:06:50,448 --> 01:06:55,468
You'll be fine.
This cave will be mine again.

408
01:06:56,143 --> 01:07:00,613
A man whose heavy injuries heal fast,
is a real valiant.

409
01:07:02,406 --> 01:07:06,046
How magnificent! You're very strong.

410
01:07:07,873 --> 01:07:11,873
I lost a lot of blood. I need strength.

411
01:07:13,259 --> 01:07:15,689
I need to stand upright, mother!

412
01:07:15,689 --> 01:07:18,739
There are a lot of enemies.
They are also harsh.

413
01:07:20,958 --> 01:07:23,328
If she's fine, it's alright.

414
01:07:23,742 --> 01:07:28,512
I want her to be in my sight.
A battle doesn't scare me.

415
01:07:45,738 --> 01:07:48,018
Still nothing from Osman, huh?

416
01:07:48,018 --> 01:07:53,048
No, father. But don't worry.
The Alps are always on the watch.

417
01:07:53,048 --> 01:07:54,638
He can't come close to the Tent.

418
01:07:54,638 --> 01:07:57,888
Batur! You still need to be careful!

419
01:07:57,888 --> 01:08:00,788
We're talking about Osman. You can't know
what he will do.

420
01:08:03,477 --> 01:08:04,907
Uncle!

421
01:08:07,169 --> 01:08:09,949
What do you think you're doing, Uncle?

422
01:08:09,949 --> 01:08:12,579
How can you let them take Osman?

423
01:08:16,832 --> 01:08:18,362
These...

424
01:08:23,799 --> 01:08:26,479
These are my fathers Beyhood symbols.

425
01:08:27,200 --> 01:08:29,740
How can you bring those
to your tent, uncle?

426
01:08:30,342 --> 01:08:32,902
What are you trying to do, uncle?

427
01:08:32,902 --> 01:08:36,902
These belong to the Kayı's
Bey, not Ertuğrul Gazi.

428
01:08:36,902 --> 01:08:40,402
So? How can you take
them before my father dies?

429
01:08:40,402 --> 01:08:44,492
You don't know the situation
since you were in Nikea.

430
01:08:45,126 --> 01:08:48,476
Now, I'm the Bey. Know your limits.

431
01:08:48,476 --> 01:08:53,176
Laws decide the limits, Dündar Bey!

432
01:08:54,679 --> 01:08:58,959
Is Kayı's throne something they
sell at the bazaar? How can you do this?

433
01:08:59,584 --> 01:09:03,174
Bey orders, Head Alp does.

434
01:09:03,733 --> 01:09:06,513
Watch your words, Gündüz Bey.

435
01:09:06,922 --> 01:09:10,162
I don't need younglings
to teach me the law!

436
01:09:18,831 --> 01:09:23,231
Don't make me a nephew killer!
Get out of my tent!

437
01:09:24,195 --> 01:09:25,695
Get out!

438
01:09:30,356 --> 01:09:34,866
Gündüz! Calm down, Gündüz.
Get a hold of yourself.

439
01:09:35,770 --> 01:09:40,050
Ayşe! I will not see you
in this tent ever again!

440
01:09:45,789 --> 01:09:50,589
From now on, we're done with this place!

441
01:10:33,642 --> 01:10:35,862
War shall wait.

442
01:10:35,866 --> 01:10:38,826
You should get better.

443
01:10:41,609 --> 01:10:45,539
Both the war and enemy don't wait.

444
01:10:46,290 --> 01:10:49,242
Those dogs bide their time to attack.

445
01:10:49,242 --> 01:10:51,402
My weapon shall be ready.

446
01:10:51,525 --> 01:10:54,735
I will not stop.

447
01:11:11,168 --> 01:11:12,958
Bala.

448
01:11:13,873 --> 01:11:15,603
Bala.

449
01:11:16,248 --> 01:11:20,318
Thank my Allah.
Look at me.

450
01:11:20,321 --> 01:11:23,121
Look at me so I celebrate it.

451
01:11:36,063 --> 01:11:40,084
You shall bring wood.
She needs to be warm.

452
01:11:40,084 --> 01:11:44,154
I would burn the mountain for her.
She shall be warm.

453
01:11:44,713 --> 01:11:48,493
You are going to get better, Bala.

454
01:11:54,483 --> 01:11:59,423
It's all going to be fine. Mother Elif
is here. I'll be right back.

455
01:12:30,058 --> 01:12:32,748
Get yourself up a little bit.

456
01:12:43,342 --> 01:12:46,022
Thank Allah you opened your eyes.

457
01:12:46,052 --> 01:12:51,062
Drink. It's healthy.
You should drink something.

458
01:12:56,161 --> 01:12:58,271
Thank you, mother.

459
01:13:07,380 --> 01:13:10,020
The pain has spread to my legs.

460
01:13:10,649 --> 01:13:12,679
They are getting numb.

461
01:13:13,845 --> 01:13:16,545
It's okay, isn't it?

462
01:13:18,964 --> 01:13:22,524
Your legs are going to be fine,
in sha Allah.

463
01:13:26,255 --> 01:13:28,205
What about the rest?

464
01:13:32,702 --> 01:13:34,592
Tell me.

465
01:13:38,534 --> 01:13:40,514
I don't want it anymore.

466
01:13:42,231 --> 01:13:44,341
You are not telling me.

467
01:13:44,954 --> 01:13:48,324
Tell me what you are hiding, mother.

468
01:13:57,503 --> 01:14:00,253
I did my best.

469
01:14:00,516 --> 01:14:03,789
And Allah allowed you and didn't take
your life.

470
01:14:03,789 --> 01:14:08,269
However, your wound is in a bad place.

471
01:14:09,161 --> 01:14:15,061
Some wounds leave a trace on the body,
while some in the soul.

472
01:14:15,746 --> 01:14:18,806
Your wound is in your soul.

473
01:14:20,539 --> 01:14:27,079
Look, my daughter, if you question why
in this universe, you will get nowhere.

474
01:14:28,605 --> 01:14:33,235
The doors will open to those who consent.

475
01:14:34,835 --> 01:14:37,525
What do you mean, mother?

476
01:14:37,706 --> 01:14:40,656
Say it directly.

477
01:14:41,853 --> 01:14:48,633
Obviously, warrior girl, you can't
have children.

478
01:14:52,742 --> 01:14:54,942
How?

479
01:15:01,531 --> 01:15:03,681
Destiny.

480
01:15:03,682 --> 01:15:07,672
I don't know if your situation recover.

481
01:15:08,196 --> 01:15:11,556
Allah is the owner of miracles.

482
01:15:13,605 --> 01:15:17,605
Mother Sahre became a mother in
ninety years old.

483
01:15:18,108 --> 01:15:22,628
Maybe a Hatun whose uterus doesn't work
have children.

484
01:15:23,881 --> 01:15:26,021
Only Allah knows.

485
01:15:26,874 --> 01:15:29,464
What are you talking about, mother?

486
01:15:30,276 --> 01:15:32,326
What are you talking about?

487
01:16:37,103 --> 01:16:41,253
I will flare the fire up.
I will warm here.

488
01:17:29,872 --> 01:17:37,182
Take me to dark souls, shaman drum.

489
01:17:49,992 --> 01:17:55,242
Dark souls shall hear my oath.

490
01:17:56,238 --> 01:18:04,658
They shall take my soul to the Erlik
Han's dark palace, with dark mud and iron.

491
01:18:06,732 --> 01:18:10,692
My oath is for Erlik Han.

492
01:18:13,137 --> 01:18:17,735
Erlik Han, this is Balgay's oath for you.

493
01:18:17,735 --> 01:18:23,655
I will irrigate your palace with that
Turk, Osman.

494
01:18:25,370 --> 01:18:32,170
I will sacrifice his soul for you, I will
give his body to ravens.

495
01:18:32,509 --> 01:18:39,229
Listen to Balgay's voice that reaches to
you via the shaman drum.

496
01:18:43,799 --> 01:18:49,909
You shall show me Osman.

497
01:19:00,851 --> 01:19:04,751
If I don't keep my promise...

498
01:19:04,751 --> 01:19:12,111
May blue sky and dark wind take my
soul.

499
01:19:16,465 --> 01:19:20,225
My soul shall...

500
01:19:21,056 --> 01:19:27,966
suffer in pain forever.

501
01:19:29,225 --> 01:19:32,695
Erlik Han...

502
01:19:34,025 --> 01:19:38,745
Give me Osman!

503
01:19:41,752 --> 01:19:44,302
Mother Elif is strange.

504
01:19:44,387 --> 01:19:48,250
Not grim, and not absolutely harsh.

505
01:19:48,250 --> 01:19:50,579
However, she is useful.

506
01:19:50,579 --> 01:19:54,859
Moreover, she will make you poultice.

507
01:19:58,714 --> 01:20:00,984
Smile please.

508
01:20:01,425 --> 01:20:03,775
It's all gone.

509
01:20:03,832 --> 01:20:06,902
We have a lot of trouble and enemy.

510
01:20:07,611 --> 01:20:11,841
Our only aim is to hold onto each other.

511
01:20:12,540 --> 01:20:15,427
Once we get rid of those troubles

512
01:20:15,427 --> 01:20:20,877
I will want you in marriage from
my Sheik.

513
01:20:22,244 --> 01:20:25,404
We will have a great garden.

514
01:20:25,887 --> 01:20:28,651
We will have children.

515
01:20:28,651 --> 01:20:34,711
We will accrue so that we gain power.

516
01:20:37,214 --> 01:20:39,954
Once you get out of this situation...

517
01:20:41,048 --> 01:20:43,928
the rest is destiny, Osman.

518
01:20:45,619 --> 01:20:49,949
It is obvious that you have difficult ways
in front of you.

519
01:20:50,567 --> 01:20:54,257
However, you will be stronger with
your children.

520
01:20:54,924 --> 01:20:58,054
Everyone will hear about Osman's
sons.

521
01:20:58,086 --> 01:21:02,816
They will know about you. You will
forget the pain.

522
01:21:05,168 --> 01:21:10,438
Your journey will be magnificent like you.

523
01:21:11,532 --> 01:21:16,232
- May Allah give you the victory.
- What is that about, Bala Hatun?

524
01:21:17,075 --> 01:21:19,895
You speak like you are leaving me.

525
01:21:21,667 --> 01:21:25,567
I pray for our journey to be together.

526
01:21:25,664 --> 01:21:27,964
Why do you speak like that?

527
01:21:28,796 --> 01:21:33,956
I'd die for you, Osman.

528
01:21:35,353 --> 01:21:38,703
Of course I will stand by you.

529
01:21:39,965 --> 01:21:41,885
Destiny.

530
01:21:42,868 --> 01:21:49,318
You have pain. I know that
you'll smile when you get better.

531
01:21:50,173 --> 01:21:53,398
Everything is going to be fine.

532
01:21:53,398 --> 01:21:57,578
These difficult days will be gone.
May my Allah give us...

533
01:21:58,185 --> 01:22:01,935
daughters and sons.

534
01:22:03,921 --> 01:22:10,371
If I am their father, I want you to be
their mother as well.

535
01:22:12,785 --> 01:22:17,050
Inshallah this will happen.
Inshallah.

536
01:22:17,050 --> 01:22:18,620
Amin.

537
01:22:18,651 --> 01:22:20,971
Don't think about me, Osman.

538
01:22:22,246 --> 01:22:26,496
They say, "Men plan god laughs."

539
01:22:29,560 --> 01:22:35,510
Allah is great.
May he give you what you want.

540
01:22:37,000 --> 01:22:40,820
Eeh, I understand, I understand.

541
01:22:40,890 --> 01:22:43,440
You will be delicate when you are sick.

542
01:22:43,918 --> 01:22:48,308
It's okay.
It's no problem when it's about you.

543
01:22:54,510 --> 01:22:56,330
Mother Elif.

544
01:22:59,571 --> 01:23:02,181
Bala Hatun is entrusted to you.

545
01:23:02,668 --> 01:23:07,108
- Take her to her father.
- Who is her father? Where can I find?

546
01:23:07,933 --> 01:23:10,923
Bala Hatun will show you the way.

547
01:23:13,662 --> 01:23:15,932
He is Sheik Edebalı.

548
01:23:16,875 --> 01:23:19,499
Sheik Edebalı?

549
01:23:19,649 --> 01:23:24,919
Allah will give me his beloved creature's
praying.

550
01:24:55,175 --> 01:24:59,455
My Sheik, you have been up for all night.
You are tired.

551
01:25:00,071 --> 01:25:05,751
They will surely find both Osman and
Bala Hatun. You should have some rest.

552
01:25:07,898 --> 01:25:12,798
- Our Allah is greater than our trouble.
- Of course.

553
01:25:12,899 --> 01:25:16,179
Of course he is the one.

554
01:25:17,981 --> 01:25:20,201
Right, Gonca daughter?

555
01:25:21,368 --> 01:25:26,228
Like you say, my Sheik.
My Allah is greater than our trouble.

556
01:25:26,252 --> 01:25:29,272
But I am desperate.

557
01:25:31,692 --> 01:25:33,972
I think of Bala.

558
01:25:35,291 --> 01:25:41,451
We always think of Bala.

559
01:25:42,002 --> 01:25:47,832
However, if there is an examination,
there is always a help

560
01:25:48,077 --> 01:25:50,847
You shall relax.

561
01:25:57,980 --> 01:26:01,154
- Bala!
- Bala, my daughter!

562
01:26:01,154 --> 01:26:04,554
Thank Allah, come here. Come.

563
01:26:04,697 --> 01:26:07,627
- She is wounded, be careful.
- Easy, easy.

564
01:26:08,228 --> 01:26:13,148
Easy, come daughter, easy.

565
01:26:13,197 --> 01:26:16,744
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)

566
01:26:16,744 --> 01:26:18,792
Thank Allah.

567
01:26:18,792 --> 01:26:21,752
Thank my Allah.

568
01:26:25,791 --> 01:26:28,981
May Allah bless you, Hatun.

569
01:26:32,328 --> 01:26:35,228
You united me and my daughter.

570
01:26:35,311 --> 01:26:38,611
May Allah give you what you want.

571
01:26:38,611 --> 01:26:45,081
I don't want anything else than a prayer
of a saint like you, Sheik Edeblaı.

572
01:26:46,721 --> 01:26:49,971
I brought Osman Bey's greetings as well.

573
01:26:51,127 --> 01:26:54,127
He is valiant.

574
01:26:54,290 --> 01:26:56,160
Yes he is.

575
01:26:57,744 --> 01:27:02,104
You shall sit, Hatun.
Catch your breath.

576
01:27:07,476 --> 01:27:12,926
Tell me, what is Osman Bey's situation?

577
01:27:43,538 --> 01:27:45,668
Get up.

578
01:28:06,052 --> 01:28:12,972
I told you where to find Osman and Edebalı.

579
01:28:26,369 --> 01:28:29,479
I told the truth.

580
01:28:36,077 --> 01:28:38,897
I want you more.

581
01:28:40,225 --> 01:28:42,685
I kept my promise.

582
01:28:42,769 --> 01:28:46,794
My son is under your guard, from now on.

583
01:28:46,794 --> 01:28:51,494
-What do you want more?
- Shut up, woman, shut up!

584
01:28:51,777 --> 01:28:59,187
Who told Geyhatu that I have Cengiz
Han's laws?

585
01:29:03,101 --> 01:29:05,241
I don't know.

586
01:29:07,257 --> 01:29:12,927
Cerkutay, bring this woman's son Batur
at once.

587
01:29:13,053 --> 01:29:19,993
I will make a crib out of his skin and
swing his mother in it.

588
01:29:21,195 --> 01:29:26,945
No, stop. No, I said stop.
Stop, stop, stop.

589
01:29:27,215 --> 01:29:29,139
Talk.

590
01:29:29,592 --> 01:29:33,542
Talk!
Who!

591
01:29:33,651 --> 01:29:40,541
Who told Geyhatu that I have Cengiz Han's
laws?

592
01:29:40,577 --> 01:29:42,677
Who?

593
01:29:43,303 --> 01:29:50,823
I am asking you for the last time.
Either you tell me that dog's name...

594
01:29:50,917 --> 01:29:56,497
or I will give Batu's head to you and
bury you alive.

595
01:29:57,144 --> 01:29:58,380
Who?

596
01:29:58,380 --> 01:30:02,651
Those are my father's Beyship signs.
How can you take them to your tent, uncle?

597
01:30:02,651 --> 01:30:06,551
Those do not belong to Ertuğrul Bey,
but to the Kayı Bey.

598
01:30:06,551 --> 01:30:09,035
How can you take them while
my father is still alive?

599
01:30:09,035 --> 01:30:13,145
You don't know about things because
you were away.

600
01:30:13,971 --> 01:30:16,141
Gündüz.

601
01:30:26,530 --> 01:30:29,440
Osman's brother Gündüz?

602
01:30:29,762 --> 01:30:32,046
Yes, he is.

603
01:30:32,046 --> 01:30:36,246
Two days ago, he left the tribe.

604
01:30:37,540 --> 01:30:40,270
We thought he went to Nike.

605
01:30:40,708 --> 01:30:43,498
But he went to Konya.

606
01:30:43,903 --> 01:30:50,573
He brought Commander Köni and his
Nökers (soldiers) to the tribe.

607
01:30:59,960 --> 01:31:01,990
I told you.

608
01:31:02,185 --> 01:31:04,575
What do you want more?

609
01:31:05,176 --> 01:31:07,396
What about Osman.

610
01:31:08,743 --> 01:31:11,133
I don't know about Osman.

611
01:31:12,579 --> 01:31:16,169
Who is close to Osman in the tribe?

612
01:31:21,123 --> 01:31:25,103
Samsa Bey and Bamsı Bey are close to Osman.

613
01:31:25,169 --> 01:31:27,829
Osman is with them.

614
01:31:27,829 --> 01:31:31,354
How can they be?
Osman and Samsa are enemies.

615
01:31:31,354 --> 01:31:35,594
They know how to unite against
the enemy.

616
01:31:54,479 --> 01:31:56,933
If you find Samsa...

617
01:31:56,933 --> 01:31:59,723
you will find Osman, Balgay.

618
01:32:02,410 --> 01:32:05,410
I know where Samsa is.

619
01:32:07,333 --> 01:32:13,783
Cerkutay, tell Kongor to kill them all
with his best Nökers (soldiers).

620
01:32:13,997 --> 01:32:21,447
I want Osman and Cengiz Han's laws alive.
Bring them to Kulucahisar Castle.

621
01:32:29,107 --> 01:32:33,517
Why are you still here, woman?
Get out!

622
01:32:40,491 --> 01:32:50,531
Blood.

623
01:33:04,880 --> 01:33:05,790
People are coming.

624
01:33:23,022 --> 01:33:23,952
Are there any news?

625
01:33:25,073 --> 01:33:25,973
Unfortunately, no.

626
01:33:32,712 --> 01:33:33,452
My sons!

627
01:33:34,268 --> 01:33:34,988
My sons!

628
01:33:35,508 --> 01:33:39,508
Just as Osman didn't surrender to those
savages in Konya...

629
01:33:39,508 --> 01:33:43,158
...we won't surrender to laziness.

630
01:33:44,839 --> 01:33:48,189
We must do everything to save our Osman.

631
01:34:43,473 --> 01:34:44,193
My Osman!

632
01:34:45,702 --> 01:34:46,412
My Bey!

633
01:34:55,399 --> 01:34:57,229
My Rab has answered to our prayers.

634
01:34:57,406 --> 01:34:58,106
My Osman!

635
01:34:59,297 --> 01:35:01,497
Oh, thank you my Rab!

636
01:35:04,053 --> 01:35:04,923
Praise Allah!

637
01:35:08,371 --> 01:35:10,041
My Bey!

638
01:35:11,475 --> 01:35:12,825
How mighty!

639
01:35:12,825 --> 01:35:15,325
Thanks to our Allah.

640
01:35:15,325 --> 01:35:16,325
My Bey!

641
01:35:19,674 --> 01:35:21,584
Allah is with us!

642
01:35:32,994 --> 01:35:35,364
Are you guys okay, huh?

643
01:35:35,364 --> 01:35:36,384
My Bey!

644
01:35:37,264 --> 01:35:37,974
My Bey!

645
01:35:38,421 --> 01:35:40,101
I knew nothing would happen to you!

646
01:35:40,101 --> 01:35:40,881
I knew it!

647
01:35:43,369 --> 01:35:44,709
Ah! My Konur!

648
01:36:07,285 --> 01:36:08,205
Bamsı Bey!

649
01:36:19,946 --> 01:36:20,906
I hope you are okay.

650
01:36:21,126 --> 01:36:22,706
Thanks to you, Bamsı Bey.

651
01:36:23,752 --> 01:36:24,732
Thanks to you.

652
01:36:29,013 --> 01:36:29,883
My Osman!

653
01:36:29,883 --> 01:36:30,753
Abdurrahman Ghazi!

654
01:36:30,772 --> 01:36:31,662
My Osman!

655
01:36:48,268 --> 01:36:49,048
My Osman.

656
01:37:04,887 --> 01:37:05,877
Abdurrahman Ghazi...

657
01:37:06,925 --> 01:37:08,945
...how's the situation at the Tent?

658
01:37:09,046 --> 01:37:11,966
We found out Dündar Bey was the one who
betrayed us.

659
01:37:13,676 --> 01:37:16,406
It seems like my uncle has sold his soul
to Mongol dogs!

660
01:37:17,761 --> 01:37:21,791
He thinks the only way to save my life
is cooperating with Geyhatu.

661
01:37:22,921 --> 01:37:24,921
So it seems the news that went to Konya...

662
01:37:24,921 --> 01:37:26,841
...didn't go there to save your life.

663
01:37:28,009 --> 01:37:30,489
He tried drive a wedge between Balgay and
Geyhatu...

664
01:37:31,448 --> 01:37:32,588
...as he sees it.

665
01:37:34,769 --> 01:37:38,599
We can't accomplish anything with
laziness, questions, and lies!

666
01:37:40,299 --> 01:37:42,389
It's certain who our enemies are!

667
01:37:43,729 --> 01:37:46,859
My uncle has been drinking from the
Byzantine fountains lately.

668
01:37:47,515 --> 01:37:49,115
If one can't fight like an Alp...

669
01:37:49,637 --> 01:37:52,137
...one must know when to step aside.

670
01:38:01,294 --> 01:38:03,364
You look thoughtful, Bamsı Bey.

671
01:38:04,433 --> 01:38:05,593
I hope it's for good.

672
01:38:06,996 --> 01:38:08,156
My Osman.

673
01:38:08,275 --> 01:38:11,805
I heard Samsa met one of the Mongol
commanders.

674
01:38:12,285 --> 01:38:13,735
I can't stop thinking of this.

675
01:38:18,783 --> 01:38:22,783
So it seems Balgay will try to negotiate
with Samsa Bey.

676
01:38:36,122 --> 01:38:38,262
Samsa Bey has evacuated his Tent, my Bey.

677
01:38:38,410 --> 01:38:40,650
It seems he went to mountains with his
Alps.

678
01:38:42,404 --> 01:38:43,274
Selamün aleyküm.

679
01:38:44,564 --> 01:38:45,664
Aleyküm selam.

680
01:38:46,558 --> 01:38:47,278
Sofia...

681
01:38:47,862 --> 01:38:50,432
...knows Samsa Bey is present at
Şahin Hill, my Bey.

682
01:38:54,827 --> 01:38:56,527
Sofia will try to provoke Balgay.

683
01:38:59,648 --> 01:39:01,268
Samsa Bey is in danger.

684
01:39:01,495 --> 01:39:03,435
We need to save him as soon as possible.

685
01:39:06,314 --> 01:39:08,604
We will ambush them in such a way...

686
01:39:09,945 --> 01:39:12,065
...that we will hit two birds with one
stone.

687
01:39:14,090 --> 01:39:16,630
Both Balgay and Sofia.

688
01:39:18,849 --> 01:39:20,319
My Bey.

689
01:39:20,826 --> 01:39:22,176
Sofia is smart.

690
01:39:23,016 --> 01:39:25,006
Do you think she will get tricked?

691
01:39:25,481 --> 01:39:27,031
She must be alert by now.

692
01:39:33,342 --> 01:39:34,182
Sıddık...

693
01:39:35,495 --> 01:39:38,475
Will become Salvador and tell her where
Sheikh Edebali is.

694
01:39:41,625 --> 01:39:43,235
She can't resist this bait.

695
01:40:52,186 --> 01:40:53,026
My Bey.

696
01:40:54,594 --> 01:40:56,394
Did you evacuate women and children?

697
01:40:56,572 --> 01:40:58,372
Alps are taking care of that, my Bey.

698
01:40:58,372 --> 01:40:59,522
It won't take much time.

699
01:40:59,695 --> 01:41:01,145
Why are you not guiding them?

700
01:41:01,329 --> 01:41:02,099
My Bey.

701
01:41:02,227 --> 01:41:05,677
I want to fight and become a martyr if
you'll allow me..

702
01:41:09,230 --> 01:41:11,380
The Hill of Martyrs is full, my Valiant.

703
01:41:11,888 --> 01:41:13,938
And there won't be space anytime soon.

704
01:41:13,988 --> 01:41:15,148
I need you alive...

705
01:41:16,239 --> 01:41:21,169
...so that we can fight against
persecutions side by side.

706
01:41:21,700 --> 01:41:24,910
So many people will get warm with the fire
of freedom we will light.

707
01:41:25,207 --> 01:41:26,907
And many savages will burn.

708
01:41:28,842 --> 01:41:31,412
We will save ummah before they lose their
hope...

709
01:41:31,612 --> 01:41:34,462
...with Turkish justice even it means we
die while fighting.

710
01:41:37,573 --> 01:41:40,673
But while we are alive we won't give
any of our soil to heathens.

711
01:41:41,020 --> 01:41:45,020
Our enemies has gathered together to fight
against all Turks.

712
01:41:46,150 --> 01:41:48,450
But there is one thing they forgot.

713
01:41:48,768 --> 01:41:50,558
If they have evil on their side.

714
01:41:51,706 --> 01:41:53,426
Turks will not stop fighting!

715
01:41:53,525 --> 01:41:54,675
Allahu Akbar!

716
01:41:54,993 --> 01:42:03,899
Allahu Akbar!

717
01:42:25,354 --> 01:42:26,364
Zöhre Hatun!

718
01:42:28,277 --> 01:42:29,227
Come here.

719
01:42:37,322 --> 01:42:38,272
Sit down.

720
01:42:44,726 --> 01:42:46,156
Let's talk for a while.

721
01:42:48,076 --> 01:42:51,536
I'm doing nothing but keeping myself busy
with this.

722
01:42:52,482 --> 01:42:54,642
After all my heart beats like a bird.

723
01:42:55,464 --> 01:42:56,874
Trouble after trouble.

724
01:42:58,774 --> 01:43:00,704
What have you been up to?

725
01:43:00,855 --> 01:43:02,615
Where did you come from?

726
01:43:04,923 --> 01:43:06,543
My Aygül doesn't feel well.

727
01:43:06,618 --> 01:43:08,958
I went to find some mint but I couldn't
find any.

728
01:43:08,958 --> 01:43:10,358
So I only picked these up.

729
01:43:10,428 --> 01:43:12,368
I already had some linden at my Tent.

730
01:43:12,368 --> 01:43:13,908
So I came back to boil some.

731
01:43:16,313 --> 01:43:18,583
May Allah give health to your daughter.

732
01:43:19,056 --> 01:43:19,946
Thank you.

733
01:43:22,547 --> 01:43:24,677
What do you think about the Tent, Zöhre?

734
01:43:25,709 --> 01:43:28,159
Perhaps you understand more than me.

735
01:43:28,924 --> 01:43:31,744
You must know what is on Dündar Bey's
mind.

736
01:43:38,055 --> 01:43:40,505
Only Allah knows about our end, Selcan
Hatun.

737
01:43:40,725 --> 01:43:43,335
We can't know what Dündar Bey is thinking.

738
01:43:43,882 --> 01:43:47,882
Can't you see he is fighting with both
Mongols and Osman.

739
01:43:49,718 --> 01:43:50,458
So...

740
01:43:51,589 --> 01:43:53,079
...you don't know yet.

741
01:43:57,011 --> 01:43:58,881
Do you know what happened?

742
01:43:59,428 --> 01:44:02,848
They found the fardel you sent Batur in
the forest.

743
01:44:04,521 --> 01:44:05,611
In the forest?

744
01:44:06,836 --> 01:44:08,046
You gave it to me.

745
01:44:08,551 --> 01:44:13,171
And I gave it to Bala after I told her
it's from you.

746
01:44:13,934 --> 01:44:14,734
So?

747
01:44:15,445 --> 01:44:16,635
So...

748
01:44:17,551 --> 01:44:19,351
...there were blood everywhere.

749
01:44:19,640 --> 01:44:21,830
And the fardel stands at some corner.

750
01:44:26,590 --> 01:44:27,590
Did she die?

751
01:44:28,939 --> 01:44:30,499
May Allah forbid that.

752
01:44:31,825 --> 01:44:33,315
Bala Hatun is lost.

753
01:44:41,422 --> 01:44:43,882
May Allah allow us to find her as soon as
possible.

754
01:44:44,938 --> 01:44:46,468
We may tell Dündar Bey.

755
01:44:46,570 --> 01:44:48,660
Maybe he can do something about this..

756
01:44:49,199 --> 01:44:49,929
No.

757
01:44:50,019 --> 01:44:50,939
Thank you.

758
01:44:51,399 --> 01:44:53,189
We must not tell Dündar Bey at all.

759
01:44:56,257 --> 01:44:58,047
They are looking for her everywhere.

760
01:44:58,047 --> 01:45:00,097
Ahis will find her if Allah helps them.

761
01:45:01,509 --> 01:45:03,299
May Allah be with them, Selcan Hatun.

762
01:45:04,070 --> 01:45:05,770
May Allah be with them.

763
01:45:07,220 --> 01:45:08,270
Good.

764
01:45:09,922 --> 01:45:12,812
Let us know if you get any news.

765
01:45:30,813 --> 01:45:33,963
May our Mother Mary protect you, Sofia.

766
01:45:34,832 --> 01:45:40,532
May she give you extra strength to destroy
our enemies for our cause.

767
01:45:51,565 --> 01:45:56,575
Today we will reach our destiny for which
we waited for too long.

768
01:45:56,865 --> 01:45:58,765
In the name of Master Yannis!

769
01:46:00,363 --> 01:46:04,363
This will cut down all the obstacles you
will come across.

770
01:46:04,633 --> 01:46:06,563
In the name of Master Yannis!

771
01:46:10,330 --> 01:46:16,210
Master Yannis, I will bring Osman who
has recently fallen from grace.

772
01:46:17,249 --> 01:46:20,799
He will pay the price of what he did to
us.

773
01:46:22,131 --> 01:46:24,981
You are the leaders of my army.

774
01:46:25,739 --> 01:46:27,859
First, Princess Sofia.

775
01:46:34,622 --> 01:46:35,832
Then, Andreas.

776
01:46:40,062 --> 01:46:41,842
And, you Helen.

777
01:46:45,209 --> 01:46:46,719
And of course...

778
01:46:49,026 --> 01:46:49,996
...Salvador.

779
01:46:51,019 --> 01:46:53,529
Today is also your day of Destiny.

780
01:46:56,821 --> 01:46:59,051
You'll get you share from our victory.

781
01:47:03,405 --> 01:47:06,105
Or from our crushing strength.

782
01:47:06,925 --> 01:47:09,185
I'm ready to give my life for our cause,
Master.

783
01:47:12,562 --> 01:47:13,972
My children.

784
01:47:14,705 --> 01:47:15,695
Rise!

785
01:47:17,590 --> 01:47:20,370
Go and arm your swords!

786
01:47:21,542 --> 01:47:25,542
Destroy all the obstacles on our path!

787
01:47:27,081 --> 01:47:29,311
Capture Osman dead or alive!

788
01:47:29,473 --> 01:47:31,073
And bring him to me!

789
01:47:31,073 --> 01:47:31,813
Go now!

790
01:47:31,813 --> 01:47:34,173
Godspeed!

791
01:47:34,343 --> 01:47:36,133
In the name of Master Yannis!

792
01:48:37,000 --> 01:48:38,800
Samsa!

793
01:48:39,623 --> 01:48:41,243
You death has arrived!

794
01:48:41,907 --> 01:48:42,807
It's shahada!

795
01:48:42,807 --> 01:48:43,677
Shahada!

796
01:48:46,548 --> 01:48:48,368
And it's our duty!

797
01:48:49,312 --> 01:48:50,412
Allahu Akbar!

798
01:49:23,284 --> 01:49:24,484
My Bey!

799
01:49:27,764 --> 01:49:28,614
Çetin Han!

800
01:49:29,272 --> 01:49:30,122
Çetin Han!

801
01:49:30,706 --> 01:49:31,526
Çetin!

802
01:49:32,027 --> 01:49:32,977
Talk to me!

803
01:49:34,479 --> 01:49:35,649
Resist, my brother!

804
01:50:06,178 --> 01:50:07,038
Samsa.

805
01:50:29,453 --> 01:50:31,173
We are here, Samsa Bey!

806
01:51:38,397 --> 01:51:39,367
Samsa Bey!

807
01:52:14,608 --> 01:52:16,618
All the persecutions you have committed...

808
01:52:16,657 --> 01:52:18,897
...did you think you could get away from
them?

809
01:52:34,081 --> 01:52:38,081
Tens of our Martyr's blood are on your
hands!

810
01:52:44,944 --> 01:52:46,994
Did you think we would forgive...

811
01:52:47,414 --> 01:52:48,644
...and forget?

812
01:53:23,738 --> 01:53:25,808
I will drown you in your own blood.

813
01:54:00,332 --> 01:54:01,102
Stop!

814
01:54:29,052 --> 01:54:30,662
What did you bring me, Sofia?

815
01:54:44,484 --> 01:54:47,034
Who are those people who want to spoil me?

816
01:54:47,277 --> 01:54:49,257
Minor rulers around our city...

817
01:54:49,412 --> 01:54:53,902
...sent these gifts to reveal their
loyalty to you.

818
01:54:54,899 --> 01:54:59,389
I will host those rulers and you in my
castle tonight.

819
01:55:01,348 --> 01:55:05,348
Did they send all these gold because they
are afraid to come to my Tent ?

820
01:55:06,273 --> 01:55:07,653
Maybe, maybe not.

821
01:55:08,546 --> 01:55:10,336
Just like we wanted.

822
01:55:11,070 --> 01:55:13,650
They sought asylum under my roof because
they fear you.

823
01:55:14,593 --> 01:55:16,833
We pull their strings from now on.

824
01:55:17,946 --> 01:55:19,436
All of them are scared.

825
01:55:20,489 --> 01:55:21,749
And hopeless.

826
01:55:22,529 --> 01:55:25,909
What else can they do...

827
01:55:26,149 --> 01:55:28,119
...except obeying mighty Balgay.

828
01:55:36,431 --> 01:55:37,981
Two of my best scouts...

829
01:55:37,981 --> 01:55:39,881
...will guide you through Şahin Hill...

830
01:55:39,881 --> 01:55:42,731
...to find Samsa Bey.

831
01:55:42,943 --> 01:55:43,883
Is that so?

832
01:55:47,023 --> 01:55:48,273
You come here!

833
01:56:01,900 --> 01:56:03,700
Who's that imbecile?

834
01:56:04,692 --> 01:56:07,392
Osman's most-trusted man.

835
01:56:11,227 --> 01:56:14,245
So that you're the one who entered
into Osman's command and...

836
01:56:14,445 --> 01:56:16,435
made him believe that you're a Muslim.

837
01:56:16,493 --> 01:56:19,083
Yes, mighty Balgay.

838
01:56:20,743 --> 01:56:23,793
Do you know where Osman is?

839
01:56:25,708 --> 01:56:27,838
No, mighty Balgay.

840
01:56:28,218 --> 01:56:31,828
But I know where Edebalı is.

841
01:56:31,867 --> 01:56:36,167
While your commanders get through
with Samsa in Şahin Hill...

842
01:56:36,639 --> 01:56:39,399
I'll take Edebalı.

843
01:56:51,349 --> 01:56:56,589
My warrior queen Sofia.

844
01:56:57,169 --> 01:57:00,873
I'll bring Edebalı's and his
daughter's heads to you...

845
01:57:00,873 --> 01:57:07,053
in the presence of landlords' tonight.

846
01:57:09,046 --> 01:57:14,936
I hope your nökers (soldiers) bring
Osman's Alps' heads.

847
01:57:23,371 --> 01:57:29,261
Today is the day of blood, Sofia.

848
01:57:30,800 --> 01:57:34,800
Dark spirits are so hungry that...

849
01:57:39,602 --> 01:57:43,602
it won't be easy at all to feed them...

850
01:57:44,053 --> 01:57:48,053
without finding Osman.

851
01:58:02,514 --> 01:58:04,704
Take his tongue!

852
01:58:06,192 --> 01:58:08,852
I'll lance his mind before his body.

853
01:58:08,991 --> 01:58:10,751
Let's see what he knows.

854
01:58:10,782 --> 01:58:14,782
You don't know who you go against.

855
01:58:14,977 --> 01:58:18,977
You'll know! You will!

856
01:58:20,065 --> 01:58:22,025
I'll show you.

857
01:58:33,196 --> 01:58:36,576
Alps! Take care of the wounded.

858
01:58:49,224 --> 01:58:51,274
Thanks, Osman Bey.

859
01:58:54,041 --> 01:58:56,831
You saved us.

860
01:58:58,825 --> 01:59:02,205
While the unbelievers trouble us...

861
01:59:03,125 --> 01:59:06,065
it's not good for us to separate.

862
01:59:11,265 --> 01:59:15,265
I called you naive...

863
01:59:15,743 --> 01:59:18,603
but it's obvious that I'm wrong.

864
01:59:18,899 --> 01:59:21,619
I feel bad. Give me your blessings.

865
01:59:22,589 --> 01:59:24,969
I give you my blessings.

866
01:59:25,807 --> 01:59:28,847
All the Kayı tent talks
about your bravery.

867
01:59:29,322 --> 01:59:32,882
Your bravery gave hope to
the innocents, Samsa Bey.

868
01:59:34,970 --> 01:59:38,430
I did what's right.

869
01:59:41,473 --> 01:59:45,413
The enemy is strong, the road is long.

870
01:59:47,873 --> 01:59:51,633
But I see that friends are tough.

871
01:59:53,668 --> 01:59:58,088
Thank you for your heart and weapon.

872
01:59:58,568 --> 02:00:01,632
Thank you, Osman Bey.

873
02:00:17,303 --> 02:00:19,583
Mashaallah! (Praise be)

874
02:00:21,213 --> 02:00:23,853
My valiants.

875
02:00:26,052 --> 02:00:30,052
From now on, valiants are...

876
02:00:30,666 --> 02:00:33,036
together.

877
02:00:34,517 --> 02:00:38,097
Unbelievers should be afraid now.

878
02:01:09,349 --> 02:01:12,419
My Gündüz! Where are you going?

879
02:01:15,244 --> 02:01:20,284
I sent Alps yesterday night. I still
haven't heard from them.

880
02:01:20,414 --> 02:01:22,022
I can't stay anymore.

881
02:01:22,054 --> 02:01:24,794
- I should help my brother.
- My Gündüz!

882
02:01:24,794 --> 02:01:29,104
Osman has saved himself.
He'll let you know.

883
02:01:29,178 --> 02:01:34,328
Hatun! I can't stay here
while my brother...

884
02:01:34,370 --> 02:01:37,130
fights with Mongols!

885
02:01:40,146 --> 02:01:42,736
I should help Osman.

886
02:01:44,497 --> 02:01:48,177
Ayşe. You won't go to that tent.

887
02:01:48,199 --> 02:01:52,199
You won't go anyone's tent who call
my uncle their Bey.

888
02:01:53,937 --> 02:01:57,937
My Gündüz. Please...

889
02:01:59,348 --> 02:02:02,038
Take care of yourself.

890
02:02:02,342 --> 02:02:03,842
You too, Hatun.

891
02:02:17,121 --> 02:02:19,401
Talk!

892
02:02:19,401 --> 02:02:21,851
I'll kill all of you.

893
02:02:21,904 --> 02:02:25,904
You'll understand the power of Mongols!

894
02:02:28,772 --> 02:02:32,772
Tell us what you know!

895
02:02:36,526 --> 02:02:38,586
Abbar. Stop.

896
02:02:38,859 --> 02:02:41,869
He killed so many innocents,
Konur brother.

897
02:02:42,040 --> 02:02:44,890
- We should do more to that dog.
- He is a captive.

898
02:02:45,862 --> 02:02:49,412
Whatever it is, we shouldn't
act like that.

899
02:02:49,744 --> 02:02:53,134
Leave please.
I'll make him talk.

900
02:03:19,164 --> 02:03:22,684
Who called you Kongar?

901
02:03:23,065 --> 02:03:26,435
- Who gave you this name?
- My name...

902
02:03:27,070 --> 02:03:29,440
... was given by a holy one.

903
02:03:29,639 --> 02:03:32,709
So I could be known in battles.

904
02:03:37,570 --> 02:03:40,680
- What is this on your neck?
- How should I know?

905
02:03:40,843 --> 02:03:43,263
Now tell me.

906
02:03:43,632 --> 02:03:48,012
- Why do I have the same one? Tell me!
- Are you interrogating me?

907
02:03:51,631 --> 02:03:55,711
Göktuğ! My brother!

908
02:03:57,384 --> 02:04:00,004
You're my brother!

909
02:04:01,553 --> 02:04:03,923
I am your brother!

910
02:04:05,531 --> 02:04:07,511
I'm Konur.

911
02:04:07,813 --> 02:04:09,663
Your brother Konur.

912
02:04:12,048 --> 02:04:15,138
Do you think I'm a child?

913
02:04:15,344 --> 02:04:18,404
Do you think you can fool
Kongar like this?

914
02:04:21,402 --> 02:04:26,642
How could you forget our father
who the Mongols killed?

915
02:04:27,119 --> 02:04:31,909
I'm a Mongol. Mongol! My parents died
in a battle!

916
02:04:34,132 --> 02:04:38,132
Göktuğ! They took your soul!

917
02:04:38,663 --> 02:04:40,413
They took your mind.

918
02:04:41,645 --> 02:04:45,455
How could you forget this sign...

919
02:04:47,012 --> 02:04:49,912
... and our burned down Tent. How?

920
02:04:55,536 --> 02:04:58,786
- Father?
- Konur. Göktuğ.

921
02:04:59,719 --> 02:05:01,819
Father!

922
02:05:03,048 --> 02:05:06,918
I'm a Mongol. Mongol!

923
02:05:06,999 --> 02:05:11,609
Let's assume you forgot this birthmark,
our grandfather İlptekin Alp...

924
02:05:11,609 --> 02:05:16,154
... and our mother who was killed.

925
02:05:19,453 --> 02:05:22,273
Did you forget yourself?

926
02:05:22,771 --> 02:05:26,611
Did you forget our lord we prayed...

927
02:05:28,033 --> 02:05:34,273
Did you forget our Prophet we said
we would die for? Tell me, Göktuğ!

928
02:05:38,239 --> 02:05:41,789
Did you forget them?

929
02:05:47,773 --> 02:05:49,813
Brother!

930
02:05:51,957 --> 02:05:54,837
- Brother!
- Brother!

931
02:06:04,495 --> 02:06:06,075
Brother!

932
02:06:16,280 --> 02:06:18,290
Konur Brother.

933
02:06:18,559 --> 02:06:21,069
Bring that dog here.

934
02:06:25,983 --> 02:06:27,853
Listen to me carefully.

935
02:06:27,875 --> 02:06:31,575
While I'm here, no one can hurt you.

936
02:06:31,575 --> 02:06:35,575
They can't touch you without fighting me!

937
02:06:35,731 --> 02:06:39,731
Do you understand? No one can touch you.
Don't you worry.

938
02:06:39,902 --> 02:06:43,022
Don't worry. Don't!

939
02:06:54,745 --> 02:06:58,745
Go, you Mongol dog! Move!

940
02:07:07,457 --> 02:07:09,087
Go!

941
02:07:51,520 --> 02:07:53,830
Where are you going, Gündüz?

942
02:07:55,821 --> 02:07:59,241
Do you have something to say to Geyhatu?

943
02:07:59,411 --> 02:08:01,831
What are you talking about?

944
02:08:03,473 --> 02:08:06,123
Balgay knows everything.

945
02:08:07,010 --> 02:08:08,850
You'll come with me.

946
02:08:10,389 --> 02:08:12,269
What if I don't?

947
02:08:55,745 --> 02:08:59,895
I didn't ask you if you want
to come with me.

948
02:09:01,395 --> 02:09:03,815
You will come with me, I said.

949
02:09:06,080 --> 02:09:07,460
What did I say?

950
02:09:07,904 --> 02:09:11,584
If a Mongol gives you an order...

951
02:09:12,013 --> 02:09:14,613
... you abide by it.

952
02:10:23,277 --> 02:10:27,637
- You did a good job, Salvador.
- Osman and his Alps will be here soon.

953
02:10:29,432 --> 02:10:32,192
Surround the place.

954
02:10:33,367 --> 02:10:36,387
No one will get out of here alive.

955
02:11:09,027 --> 02:11:10,877
Why?

956
02:11:11,899 --> 02:11:16,019
Why did you tell Geyhatu, Gündüz?

957
02:11:19,823 --> 02:11:21,893
Who told this to you?

958
02:11:30,294 --> 02:11:33,594
Since you made Balgay your enemy...

959
02:11:34,311 --> 02:11:36,681
... you have decided your fate.

960
02:11:42,006 --> 02:11:46,016
I don't know who is confusing you, but...

961
02:11:49,623 --> 02:11:53,623
Do you know how those...

962
02:11:54,103 --> 02:11:56,913
... who torture the Kayıs die?

963
02:11:59,224 --> 02:12:01,934
You will eventually.

964
02:12:06,042 --> 02:12:09,952
You were vicious at the moorland.
And you're the same in Söğüt.

965
02:12:14,477 --> 02:12:16,987
You changed a little bit.

966
02:12:17,357 --> 02:12:24,127
- But your behaviors are the same.
- Your hands are full of blood now, Cerkutay.

967
02:12:25,842 --> 02:12:31,432
Osman will kill you if I can't.

968
02:12:31,691 --> 02:12:35,451
You'll die all.

969
02:13:18,275 --> 02:13:21,945
- Salamun Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salaam.

970
02:13:29,317 --> 02:13:32,757
- Salamun Alaikum, my Sheikh.
- Alaikum Salaam.

971
02:13:32,838 --> 02:13:35,458
I brought you the regards of Osman Bey.

972
02:13:54,183 --> 02:13:55,423
Salvador!

973
02:13:55,794 --> 02:13:57,904
You traitor!

974
02:14:01,589 --> 02:14:03,959
Kill them all!

975
02:16:09,406 --> 02:16:11,786
It's hard to be a Turk, Sofia.

976
02:16:12,690 --> 02:16:16,690
You go against the cruel ones
because of innocent ones.

977
02:16:21,175 --> 02:16:23,645
But it's harder not to be a Turk.

978
02:16:27,489 --> 02:16:31,599
Because you go against the Turks.

979
02:16:39,163 --> 02:16:41,873
We'll kill you all.

980
02:16:51,836 --> 02:16:54,386
- Princess!
- Shut up!

981
02:17:41,276 --> 02:17:44,076
Tell everyone that...

982
02:17:44,139 --> 02:17:47,919
It doesn't matter if the seven
worlds come at us.

983
02:17:48,822 --> 02:17:52,922
Osman's war has started!

984
02:17:52,979 --> 02:17:59,889
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)

985
02:17:59,987 --> 02:18:03,197
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)